                <div class="abstract-section">
                    <div class="abstract-header">ABSTRAK</div>
                    <p class="abstract-text">
                        Artikel ini menyajikan analisis komprehensif terhadap arsitektur dan evolusi kinerja BitTrade-v2 Engine (Bot A), sistem trading algoritmik berbasis Rust yang beroperasi pada pasangan BTC/USDT dan multi-koin USDT. Sistem awal mengimplementasikan deteksi market regime (Trending/Sideways), namun analisis data operasional mengungkap kelemahan indikator konvensional yang sering menghasilkan fake-out trap. Penelitian ini mendokumentasikan transformasi arsitektural menuju Quant Professional System (QPS) melalui tiga fase utama: pengetatan parameter (Fase 4.x), integrasi Dynamic Risk Management berbasis Quarter Kelly Criterion dan Rolling Sharpe Ratio (Fase 5.0), serta modularisasi empat mesin strategi dan ekspansi multi-koin dengan klasifikasi volatilitas dinamis disertai mekanisme QPS Auto-Recovery (Fase 5.1–5.2). Auto-Recovery menghilangkan risiko operational deadlock dengan mengalihkan sistem ke mode budget minimum ($5,05/trade) saat Sharpe Ratio negatif, alih-alih menghentikan total. Hasil evaluasi backtest 16 bulan menunjukkan peningkatan Win Rate dari 26,05% menjadi 59,49% dengan penurunan Maximum Drawdown dari 71,28% menjadi 1,87%. Pengujian live pada Fase 5.2 mencatat 25 transaksi SELL berhasil dengan Win Rate 100% tanpa satu pun Stop Loss terpicu.
                    </p>
                    <p class="abstract-text">
                        <strong>Kata Kunci:</strong> trading algoritmik, kriteria kelly, rasio sharpe, ketidakseimbangan buku pesanan, kripto.
                    </p>
                </div>
                
                <div class="abstract-section" style="margin-top:25px;">
                    <div class="abstract-header">ABSTRACT</div>
                    <p class="abstract-text en-text">
                        This article presents a comprehensive analysis of the architecture and performance evolution of the BitTrade-v2 Engine (Bot A), a Rust-based algorithmic trading system operating on BTC/USDT and multi-coin USDT pairs. The system initially implemented market regime detection (Trending/Sideways), but operational data analysis revealed weaknesses in conventional indicators frequently generating fake-out traps. This research documents the architectural transformation toward the Quant Professional System (QPS) through three main phases: parameter tightening (Phase 4.x), integration of Dynamic Risk Management based on Quarter Kelly Criterion and Rolling Sharpe Ratio (Phase 5.0), and modularization of four strategy engines and multi-coin expansion with dynamic volatility classification plus the QPS Auto-Recovery mechanism (Phases 5.1–5.2). Auto-Recovery eliminates operational deadlock risk by switching the system to a minimum budget mode ($5.05/trade) when Sharpe Ratio turns negative, rather than halting execution entirely. A 16-month backtest evaluation showed Win Rate improvement from 26.05% to 59.49%, with Maximum Drawdown reduction from 71.28% to 1.87%. Live testing in Phase 5.2 recorded 25 successful SELL transactions with a 100% Win Rate and zero Stop Loss triggers.
                    </p>
                    <p class="abstract-text en-text">
                        <strong>Keywords:</strong> algorithmic trading, kelly criterion, sharpe ratio, order book imbalance, cryptocurrency.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- 1. Introduction -->
            <div class="article-section-content" id="sec-1">
                <h2 class="section-title">PENDAHULUAN <span class="en-title">/ INTRODUCTION</span></h2>
                <div class="p-pair">
                    <p class="p-id">
                        Pasar aset kripto, khususnya pasangan BTC/USDT, dicirikan oleh volatilitas ekstrim, asimetri informasi tinggi, dan kecepatan transisi kondisi pasar (market regime) yang sangat dinamis antara fase trending dan sideways. Karakteristik ini membuat pendekatan tradisional menggunakan indikator teknikal tunggal rentan menghasilkan sinyal palsu ketika kondisi pasar berubah mendadak (Kirkpatrick & Dahlquist, 2016). Sistem trading algoritmik generasi awal seperti Bot A (BitTrade-v2 Engine) dirancang untuk memitigasi kelemahan tersebut melalui deteksi market regime. Namun, data empiris nyata mengungkap fenomena sistematis: mayoritas sinyal perpotongan indikator (EMA Golden Cross) terpicu akibat manipulasi likuiditas buatan (fake-out), bukan minat fundamental pasar sesungguhnya. Eksekusi masif pada sinyal palsu ini menyebabkan kerugian kumulatif yang signifikan.
                    </p>
                    <p class="p-en">
                        The cryptocurrency market, particularly BTC/USDT, is characterized by extreme volatility, high information asymmetry, and highly dynamic market regime transitions between trending and sideways phases. These characteristics make traditional approaches using single technical indicators prone to generating false signals during sudden market transitions (Kirkpatrick & Dahlquist, 2016). Early algorithmic trading systems such as Bot A were designed to mitigate these weaknesses through market regime detection. However, real empirical data revealed a systematic phenomenon: the majority of EMA Golden Cross signals were triggered by artificial liquidity manipulation (fake-outs) rather than genuine market interest. Massive execution on these false signals caused significant cumulative losses.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="p-pair">
                    <p class="p-id">
                        Penelitian ini merumuskan dua masalah utama: (1) Bagaimana mengidentifikasi momentum pergerakan harga yang asli (genuine breakout) dari gerakan palsu (fake-out manipulation) secara real-time? (2) Bagaimana mencegah sistem mengalami kebangkrutan (ruin) pada masa transisi pasar yang dipenuhi rentetan kerugian beruntun (losing streaks)? Tujuan utama penelitian ini adalah merancang, mengimplementasikan, dan mengevaluasi arsitektur Quant Professional System (QPS) pada BitTrade-v2. Secara spesifik: (a) memformulasikan manajemen ukuran transaksi dinamis melalui Kelly Criterion yang dimodulasi oleh Sharpe Ratio; (b) mengembangkan modul High-Frequency Microstructure Analysis via kalkulasi Order Book Imbalance (OBI); dan (c) merancang arsitektur multi-koin dengan klasifikasi volatilitas dinamis untuk memperluas cakupan peluang pasar.
                    </p>
                    <p class="p-en">
                        This research formulates two main problems: (1) How to identify genuine price movement momentum from fake-out manipulation in real-time? (2) How to prevent the system from experiencing ruin during market transition periods filled with consecutive losing streaks? The primary objective is to design, implement, and evaluate the Quant Professional System (QPS) architecture on BitTrade-v2. Specifically: (a) formulate dynamic transaction size management through Kelly Criterion modulated by Sharpe Ratio; (b) develop a High-Frequency Microstructure Analysis module via Order Book Imbalance (OBI) calculation; and (c) design a multi-coin architecture with dynamic volatility classification to expand market opportunity coverage.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- 2. Lit Review -->
            <div class="article-section-content" id="sec-2">
                <h2 class="section-title">TINJAUAN PUSTAKA <span class="en-title">/ LITERATURE REVIEW</span></h2>
                
                <h3 class="subsection-title">2.1 Market Regime Detection <span class="en-subtitle">/ 2.1 Market Regime Detection</span></h3>
                <div class="p-pair">
                    <p class="p-id">
                        Deteksi market regime merupakan fondasi sistem perdagangan adaptif modern. Lo (2017) membuktikan bahwa pasar keuangan bersifat non-stasioner, bergerak bergantian antara fase momentum dan mean reversion. Pendekatan umum adalah memanfaatkan tingkat volatilitas persentase (standard deviation) sebagai ambang batas klasifikasi.
                    </p>
                    <p class="p-en">
                        Market regime detection is the foundation of modern adaptive trading systems. Lo (2017) proved that financial markets are non-stationary, alternating between momentum and mean reversion phases. A common approach uses percentage volatility (standard deviation) as a classification threshold.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <h3 class="subsection-title">2.2 Institutional Risk Management <span class="en-subtitle">/ 2.2 Institutional Risk Management</span></h3>
                <div class="p-pair">
                    <p class="p-id">
                        Kriteria Kelly adalah formula matematika yang menentukan porsi kekayaan optimal untuk dipertaruhkan pada sebuah peluang investasi (MacLean et al., 2016). Sistem profesional modern mengadopsi Fractional Kelly (khususnya Quarter Kelly) untuk mengurangi risiko kebangkrutan. Alokasi modal tidak hanya memperhitungkan win rate, melainkan juga disesuaikan dengan imbal-risiko yang direpresentasikan oleh nilai Sharpe Ratio (Bailey & Lopez de Prado, 2018; Pardo, 2020).
                    </p>
                    <p class="p-en">
                        The Kelly Criterion is a mathematical formula determining the optimal fraction of wealth to stake on an investment opportunity (MacLean et al., 2016). Modern professional systems adopt Fractional Kelly (particularly Quarter Kelly) to reduce ruin risk. Capital allocation accounts not only for win rate, but is also adjusted for risk-reward represented by the Sharpe Ratio (Bailey & Lopez de Prado, 2018; Pardo, 2020).
                    </p>
                </div>

                <h3 class="subsection-title">2.3 Market Microstructure Theory <span class="en-subtitle">/ 2.3 Market Microstructure Theory</span></h3>
                <div class="p-pair">
                    <p class="p-id">
                        Mikrostruktur pasar mempelajari proses pembentukan harga pada tingkat terendah: pencocokan setiap bid dan ask order (Cartea et al., 2015). Order Book Imbalance (OBI) adalah matriks asimetri utama yang mengungkap niat tersembunyi pasar (Cont et al., 2014). Pada aset kripto, institusi pembentuk harga (market makers) menempatkan limit order masif untuk menciptakan Sell Wall atau Buy Wall, yang dapat terdeteksi melalui rasio OBI secara real-time (Ustun & Toy, 2020).
                    </p>
                    <p class="p-en">
                        Market microstructure studies the price formation process at its lowest level: the matching of each bid and ask order (Cartea et al., 2015). Order Book Imbalance (OBI) is the primary asymmetry matrix revealing the market's hidden intentions (Cont et al., 2014). In crypto markets, market makers place massive limit orders creating Sell Walls or Buy Walls detectable through real-time OBI ratios (Ustun & Toy, 2020).
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- 3. Methodology -->
            <div class="article-section-content" id="sec-3">
                <h2 class="section-title">METODE <span class="en-title">/ METHOD</span></h2>
                
                <h3 class="subsection-title">3.1 Core Technology and System Architecture <span class="en-subtitle">/ 3.1 Core Technology and System Architecture</span></h3>
                <div class="p-pair">
                    <p class="p-id">
                        BitTrade-v2 Engine dibangun menggunakan bahasa pemrograman Rust dengan ekosistem Tokio (asynchronous runtime), memberikan jaminan keamanan memori dan kemampuan multithreading ekstrem (Blandy, 2021; Lattner, 2019). Persistensi data menggunakan PostgreSQL via sqlx. Sistem dirancang sebagai pipeline 5-tahap berbasis event-driven: (1) Ingestion, (2) Heuristic, (3) Conclude, (4) Risk & Validate, (5) Executor. Untuk memastikan transparansi dan pemantauan sistem secara langsung, data operasional dan status pipeline event-driven Bot A dipublikasikan secara real-time pada portal monitoring eksternal di <a href="https://tradingsafe.mijdigital.my/bota/" target="_blank">https://tradingsafe.mijdigital.my/bota/</a>.
                    </p>
                    <p class="p-en">
                        BitTrade-v2 Engine is built using Rust with the Tokio ecosystem (async runtime), ensuring memory safety and extreme multithreading capabilities (Blandy, 2021; Lattner, 2019). Data persistence uses PostgreSQL via sqlx. The system is designed as a 5-stage event-driven pipeline: (1) Ingestion, (2) Heuristic, (3) Conclude, (4) Risk & Validate, (5) Executor. To ensure transparency and real-time system monitoring, the operational data and event-driven pipeline status of Bot A are published in real-time on the external monitoring portal at <a href="https://tradingsafe.mijdigital.my/bota/" target="_blank">https://tradingsafe.mijdigital.my/bota/</a>.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <h3 class="subsection-title">3.2 Dynamic Risk Management <span class="en-subtitle">/ 3.2 Dynamic Risk Management</span></h3>
                <div class="p-pair">
                    <p class="p-id">
                        Modul QPS Risk menganalisis 20 transaksi SELL terakhir (Window T-20) dari basis data SQL untuk menghasilkan rata-rata pengembalian bersih per perdagangan (μ) dan volatilitas pengembalian (σ). Nilai Sharpe Ratio dan Quarter Kelly Fraction kemudian dihitung sebagai:
                    </p>
                    <p class="p-en">
                        The QPS Risk module analyzes the last 20 SELL transactions (T-20 Window) from the SQL database to produce average net return per trade (μ) and return volatility (σ). The Sharpe Ratio and Quarter Kelly Fraction are then computed as:
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="math-block">
                    <span>Sharpe = μ / σ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; f<sub>quarter</sub> = 0.25 · (μ / σ²)</span>
                    <span class="math-eq-num">(1)</span>
                </div>
                <div class="p-pair">
                    <p class="p-id">
                        Apabila Sharpe Ratio bernilai negatif, QPS mengeluarkan sinyal Capital Preservation (alokasi minimum $5,05 per perdagangan). Apabila Sharpe positif, alokasi anggaran dieksekusi berdasarkan nilai Quarter Kelly dengan batas atas dinamis maksimal 35% saldo.
                    </p>
                    <p class="p-en">
                        If Sharpe Ratio is negative, QPS issues a Capital Preservation signal (minimum $5.05 allocation per trade). If Sharpe is positive, budget allocation executes based on Quarter Kelly fraction, capped dynamically at 35% of free balance.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <h3 class="subsection-title">3.3 Order Book Imbalance Filter <span class="en-subtitle">/ 3.3 Order Book Imbalance Filter</span></h3>
                <div class="p-pair">
                    <p class="p-id">
                        Sistem memantau kuantitas volume pada antrean Best Bid dan Best Ask untuk menghitung koefisien tekanan OBI:
                    </p>
                    <p class="p-en">
                        The system monitors volume quantities in the Best Bid and Best Ask queues to calculate the OBI pressure coefficient:
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="math-block">
                    <span>OBI = Volume<sub>Bid</sub> / (Volume<sub>Bid</sub> + Volume<sub>Ask</sub>)</span>
                    <span class="math-eq-num">(2)</span>
                </div>
                <div class="p-pair">
                    <p class="p-id">
                        Ambang penolakan keras ditetapkan pada OBI &lt; 0,40 (artinya ≥60% volume antrian utama dikuasai Sell Wall), yang secara dinamis membatalkan order beli demi memitigasi jebakan fake breakout.
                    </p>
                    <p class="p-en">
                        A hard rejection threshold is set at OBI &lt; 0.40 (meaning ≥60% of main queue volume is controlled by a Sell Wall), dynamically canceling buy orders to mitigate fake breakout traps.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <h3 class="subsection-title">3.4 Multi-Coin Architecture &amp; Volatility Classification <span class="en-subtitle">/ 3.4 Multi-Coin Architecture &amp; Volatility Classification</span></h3>
                <div class="p-pair">
                    <p class="p-id">
                        Pada Fase 5.2, sistem bertransformasi dari bot single-regime berbasis EMA menjadi sistem pemantauan multi-koin asinkron yang melacak 100+ koin secara paralel. Sistem secara otomatis menghitung Standard Deviation 24 jam per koin dan mengelompokkannya ke empat tier volatilitas: EXTREME, HYPER, HIGH, dan LOW. Parameter target Trailing TP dan Pullback dikalibrasi secara adaptif berdasarkan tier tersebut:
                    </p>
                    <p class="p-en">
                        In Phase 5.2, the system transforms from a single-regime EMA-based bot to a multi-coin monitoring system tracking 100+ coins in parallel. The system automatically calculates the 24-hour Standard Deviation per coin and categorizes them into four volatility tiers: EXTREME, HYPER, HIGH, and LOW. Trailing TP target and pullback parameters are calibrated adaptively based on these tiers:
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="table-caption">Table 1. Trailing TP Parameter Configuration per Volatility Tier</div>
                <table class="academic-table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Volatility Tier</th>
                            <th>24h StdDev Threshold</th>
                            <th>Trailing TP Trigger</th>
                            <th>Trailing Pullback</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>EXTREME</strong></td>
                            <td>≥ 3.0%</td>
                            <td>3.0%</td>
                            <td>1.5%</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>HYPER</strong></td>
                            <td>1.5% – 3.0%</td>
                            <td>2.0%</td>
                            <td>1.0%</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>HIGH</strong></td>
                            <td>0.5% – 1.5%</td>
                            <td>1.5%</td>
                            <td>0.8%</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>LOW</strong></td>
                            <td>&lt; 0.5%</td>
                            <td>1.2%</td>
                            <td>0.6%</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
                <div class="table-source">Source: Simulated system backtest configuration.</div>

                <div class="p-pair" style="margin-top: 25px;">
                    <p class="p-id">
                        Setiap siklus analisis (tiap menit), sistem menjalankan pipeline seleksi 4 tahap untuk memilih 100 koin paling potensial dari 400+ pasangan USDT aktif: (1) Filter minimum (harga >0 dan volume 24h >$100.000); (2) Pemeringkatan berdasarkan StdDev 24h; (3) Bobot volume sebagai tiebreaker; (4) Batasan maksimum Top-100.
                    </p>
                    <p class="p-en">
                        Each analysis cycle (per minute), the system runs a 4-stage selection pipeline to choose the 100 most promising coins from 400+ active USDT pairs: (1) Minimum filter (price >0 and 24h volume >$100,000); (2) Ranking by 24h StdDev; (3) Volume weight as tiebreaker; (4) Top-100 maximum limit.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <h3 class="subsection-title">3.5 QPS Auto-Recovery Mode <span class="en-subtitle">/ 3.5 QPS Auto-Recovery Mode</span></h3>
                <div class="p-pair">
                    <p class="p-id">
                        Salah satu kelemahan desain QPS Fase 5.0 adalah perilaku binary halt: ketika Sharpe Ratio negatif, sistem mengembalikan alokasi 0.0 sehingga bot berhenti total. Kondisi ini berpotensi menyebabkan deadlock operasional—bot tidak pernah mengeksekusi transaksi, sehingga window T-20 tidak pernah terperbarui, dan Sharpe Ratio tidak pernah pulih secara mandiri.
                    </p>
                    <p class="p-en">
                        A key design weakness in QPS Phase 5.0 was its binary halt behavior: when Sharpe Ratio turned negative, the system returned a 0.0 allocation, causing the bot to stop completely. This created an operational deadlock—the bot never executes trades, the T-20 window never refreshes, and the Sharpe Ratio can never self-recover.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="p-pair">
                    <p class="p-id">
                        Pada Fase 5.2, mekanisme ini dirombak menjadi QPS Auto-Recovery Mode. Modul risk.rs kini mengembalikan nilai sinyal khusus -1.0 (bukan 0.0) saat Sharpe Ratio negatif. Setiap mesin strategi (breakout.rs, uptrend.rs, downtrend.rs, sideways.rs) mendeteksi sinyal ini dan menetapkan budget flat minimum sebesar $5,05 per trade—cukup untuk memenuhi batas minimum order Binance—alih-alih memblokir eksekusi total. Mekanisme ini memastikan sistem selalu beroperasi pada intensitas rendah saat kinerja sedang buruk, membangun riwayat transaksi baru agar Sharpe Ratio dapat pulih secara otomatis.
                    </p>
                    <p class="p-en">
                        In Phase 5.2, this mechanism was redesigned as the QPS Auto-Recovery Mode. The risk.rs module now returns a special signal value of -1.0 (not 0.0) when Sharpe Ratio is negative. Each strategy engine (breakout.rs, uptrend.rs, downtrend.rs, sideways.rs) detects this signal and sets a flat minimum budget of $5.05 per trade—sufficient to meet Binance's minimum order threshold—instead of blocking execution entirely. This mechanism ensures the system always operates at low intensity during poor performance periods, building new transaction history so the Sharpe Ratio can recover autonomously.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- 4. Results & Discussion -->
            <div class="article-section-content" id="sec-4">
                <h2 class="section-title">HASIL DAN PEMBAHASAN <span class="en-title">/ RESULTS AND DISCUSSION</span></h2>
                
                <h3 class="subsection-title">4.1 Pre-QPS Evaluation <span class="en-subtitle">/ 4.1 Pre-QPS Evaluation</span></h3>
                <div class="p-pair">
                    <p class="p-id">
                        Pengujian coba jalan 48 jam pada Fase 4.2 menghasilkan Win Rate 30,0% dengan Net P&L kumulatif −$12,22. Pembedahan kronologis mengungkap dua pola destruktif dominan: FOMO Re-entry Trap (re-entry pasca profit di harga mahal) dan Dead Volume Fake-out (masuk saat volume kosong). Pada Fase awal operasional QPS (Fase 5.0), sistem mencatat 0 transaksi selama 9 hari, bukan indikasi perlindungan risiko berhasil, melainkan kegagalan parameter threshold statis.
                    </p>
                    <p class="p-en">
                        The 48-hour test run in Phase 4.2 yielded a 30.0% Win Rate with cumulative Net P&L of −$12.22. Chronological dissection revealed two dominant destructive patterns: FOMO Re-entry Trap (re-entering post-profit at expensive prices) and Dead Volume Fake-out (entering when volume is empty). In the early QPS operational phase (Phase 5.0), the system recorded 0 transactions over 9 days—not indicative of successful risk protection, but rather a failure of static threshold parameters.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="math-block" style="border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-red); background-color: var(--accent-red-light); color: var(--accent-red); font-family: 'Arial Narrow', Arial, sans-serif; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px;">
                    <strong style="font-size: 11pt; letter-spacing: 1px;">CRITICAL FINDING</strong>
                    <p style="font-size: 11pt; margin: 0; line-height: 1.3; font-style: normal;">
                        Data riil membuktikan OBI level-1 jarang melampaui 0,40—faktanya >85% observasi berada di bawah 0,10. Dari 590 sinyal Golden Cross terpicu, 100% diblokir sebelum dievaluasi modul Kelly/Sharpe. Strategi Sideways tercatat 0 kali aktif akibat ambang volatilitas kaku (0,085%).
                    </p>
                    <p style="font-size: 11pt; margin: 0; line-height: 1.3; opacity: 0.85; font-style: italic;">
                        [English] Real data proved level-1 OBI rarely exceeds 0.40—in fact, >85% of observations sit below 0.10. Of 590 triggered Golden Cross signals, 100% were blocked before evaluation by the Kelly/Sharpe module. The Sideways strategy triggered 0 times due to a rigid 0.085% volatility threshold.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <h3 class="subsection-title">4.2 Qualitative Comparison <span class="en-subtitle">/ 4.2 Qualitative Comparison</span></h3>
                <div class="table-caption">Table 2. Qualitative Comparison Pre-QPS and QPS</div>
                <table class="academic-table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Evaluation Parameter</th>
                            <th>Pre-QPS (Phase 4)</th>
                            <th>QPS (Phase 5)</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Breakout Signals</strong></td>
                            <td>Vulnerable to Fake-outs</td>
                            <td>Blocked if OBI &lt; 0.40</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Entry Frequency</strong></td>
                            <td>Overtrading (18 signals/hr)</td>
                            <td>Adaptive selectivity</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Position Management</strong></td>
                            <td>Static (20% balance)</td>
                            <td>Dynamic Kelly (0%–35%)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Protection Point</strong></td>
                            <td>Rigid (-1.2% static)</td>
                            <td>Dynamic (3.0x ATR)</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
                <div class="table-source">Source: Theoretical design benchmark evaluations.</div>

                <h3 class="subsection-title" style="margin-top: 30px;">4.3 Backtest Results <span class="en-subtitle">/ 4.3 Backtest Results</span></h3>
                <div class="p-pair">
                    <p class="p-id">
                        Integrasi modular empat mesin strategi (Fase 5.1) dievaluasi menggunakan backtest 16 bulan historis. Strategi Downtrend Catcher dioptimalkan menggunakan micro take profit +0,80% dan VWAP discount ≤ −0,80%, menghasilkan Win Rate 75,0% (6 Menang / 2 Kalah). Strategi Breakout disaring melalui StdDev ≥ 30, spike ≥ 0,5%, dan OBI ≥ 0,40, meningkatkan Win Rate breakout dari 18,35% menjadi 64,71%.
                    </p>
                    <p class="p-en">
                        The modular integration of four strategy engines (Phase 5.1) was evaluated using a 16-month historical backtest. The Downtrend Catcher strategy was optimized using micro take profit +0.80% and VWAP discount ≤ −0.80%, yielding 75.0% Win Rate (6 Wins / 2 Losses). The Breakout strategy filtered through StdDev ≥ 30, spike ≥ 0.5%, and OBI ≥ 0.40 lifted breakout Win Rate from 18.35% to 64.71%.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="table-caption">Table 3. Backtest Performance Comparison: Phase 5.0 vs Phase 5.1</div>
                <table class="academic-table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Performance Metric</th>
                            <th>Phase 5.0 (Default)</th>
                            <th>Phase 5.1 (Optimized)</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Final Equity</strong></td>
                            <td>$287.20 (-71.28%)</td>
                            <td>$1,827.50 (+82.75%)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Win Rate</strong></td>
                            <td>26.05%</td>
                            <td>59.49% (47 Wins / 32 Losses)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Max Drawdown</strong></td>
                            <td>71.28%</td>
